Curriculum indicator B7.3.1.1.1
> 🎯 **Learning objectives** By the end of this lesson you should be able to:
- explain what a computer network is;
- identify key hardware used to set up networks;
- explain and draw bus, star, ring and mesh topologies, stating their features.
A **computer network** is two or more computers and other devices (printers, phones, servers) connected together so that they can **share resources** (files, printers, Internet connection) and **communicate**. Connections may be **wired** (cables) or **wireless** (radio waves such as Wi-Fi and Bluetooth).
